# Normalise line endings.
#
# You are developing on Windows (CRLF) but the backend runs in a Linux
# container (LF). Without this file, a shell script committed from Windows
# arrives in the container with CRLF and fails as:
#
#     /bin/sh^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# which is an extremely confusing error the first time you hit it.
# `text=auto` stores everything as LF in git and checks out natively.
* text=auto

# Files that must be LF even on disk, because Linux tooling reads them.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.ttf           binary
*.otf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.pdf           binary
